# Agent Architecture & Code Generation Rules

## 3-Agent Pipeline (LLM Disabled)

Generation is rule-based. The pipeline is:
1. **StepProcessor** (Agent 1) — classifies raw test steps into `ProcessedStep` with `PageContext` (tracks `currentPage`, `isEditMode`, `currentTab`, `currentApp`)
2. **POMMethodMatcher** (Agent 2) — matches steps to existing POM methods or proposes new ones using `AppSourceIndexer` data
3. **SpecValidator** (Agent 3) — validates generated spec against guardrails, auto-fixes violations (including NAV-001 for missing navigateToBaseUrl)

## Application Source Locators

The `AppSourceIndexer` scans cloned repos (`modetrans/mono.git`, `modetrans/dme.git`) for HTML elements. Cache lives in `src/agent/.cache/`.

### View Mode vs Edit Mode

- **Edit mode**: Form elements exist with exact `#id` — use `page.locator('#id')` with `.inputValue()` / `.fill()`
- **View mode**: Same fields render as plain text in `<td>` — use Playwright chained locators: `page.getByRole('row', { name: /Label/i }).locator('td').nth(1)` with `.textContent()`
- The `StepProcessor` tracks `isEditMode`; `POMMethodMatcher` uses it to choose the locator strategy

## MANDATORY: navigateToBaseUrl() Before Header Navigation

**Detail/form pages** (View Office Info, View Customer, Edit Load, View Carrier, Edit Office, etc.) do NOT render the main navigation header buttons (Admin, Customers, Loads, Finance, Home, etc.).

**Rule**: ALWAYS call `pages.basePage.navigateToBaseUrl()` BEFORE `pages.basePage.hoverOverHeaderByText()`. This is enforced at three levels:
1. **StepMappings** — all HOVER and NAVIGATION entries prepend `navigateToBaseUrl()`
2. **SpecValidator (NAV-001)** — detects and auto-fixes missing `navigateToBaseUrl()` before `hoverOverHeaderByText()`
3. **PromptsConfig guardrail** — `navigateToBaseUrlBeforeHeaderNav` rule flags violations at generation time

The call is idempotent — safe even if already on the base URL. Reference specs: BT-67846, BT-74418, DFB-97739.

```typescript
// CORRECT — always navigateToBaseUrl before header nav
await pages.basePage.navigateToBaseUrl();
await pages.basePage.hoverOverHeaderByText(HEADERS.CUSTOMER);
await pages.basePage.clickSubHeaderByText(CUSTOMER_SUB_MENU.SEARCH);

// WRONG — will fail if browser is on a detail/form page
await pages.basePage.hoverOverHeaderByText(HEADERS.CUSTOMER);
```

## MANDATORY: Billing Toggle User Switch

**All test cases in the `billingtoggle` category** MUST switch to `USER_ROLES.BILLINGTOGGLE_USER` after the initial login. This is enforced at three levels:
1. **StepMappings** — BILLINGTOGGLE_USER pattern generates the correct switch code
2. **SpecValidator (CAT-BT-001)** — detects missing `USER_ROLES.BILLINGTOGGLE_USER` in billingtoggle specs and auto-fixes by injecting the switch after `BTMSLogin`
3. **PromptsConfig** — `BILLING_TOGGLE_USER_SWITCH` rule documents the requirement

```typescript
// CORRECT — billing toggle specs
await pages.btmsLoginPage.BTMSLogin(userSetup.globalUser);
await pages.homePage.clickSwitchAccountButton();
await pages.agentAccountsPage.clickOnUserNameIfVisible(USER_ROLES.BILLINGTOGGLE_USER);

// WRONG — missing user switch (will fail CAT-BT-001)
await pages.btmsLoginPage.BTMSLogin(userSetup.globalUser);
```

The constant `USER_ROLES.BILLINGTOGGLE_USER` is defined in `globalConstants.ts`. NEVER hardcode the username string directly. Reference spec: BT-74421.

## Billing toggle: View Load vs View Billing (Waiting On / finance)

When generating or editing **billingtoggle** (and similar load-finance) tests, follow the **same POM layer and order as the canonical spec** `src/tests/AIAgent/billingtoggle/BT-74454.spec.ts` (also listed first in `REFERENCE_SPECS.billingtoggle` / `ReferenceSpecAnalyzer`).

| Surface | DOM / source | POM | Read Waiting On |
|--------|----------------|-----|------------------|
| **View Load → Load tab** | `loadform.php`: **`select#fi_waiting_on`** (option values `Agent` / `Billing`, strings) | `ViewLoadPage` | `clickloadTab()`, `scrollWaitingOnIntoView()`, `getBillingIssuesWaitingOnDisplayLabel()` — assert with `PAYABLE_TOGGLE_VALUE.*` |
| **View Billing** | `billing.php`: **`#finance_issues_block`**, hidden `#fi_waiting_on` (numeric 1/2/3) + slider | `LoadBillingPage` | `scrollBillingIssuesBlockIntoView()`, `getBillingToggleValue()`, `isNotDeliveredFinalChecked()`, finance message helpers |

**Rules**

1. **After Save on Edit Load** when the testcase says **View Load** (or the app returns to View Load): validate Waiting On with **`ViewLoadPage`**, not `LoadBillingPage.getBillingToggleValue()`.
2. **After View Billing** is open: use **`LoadBillingPage`** for `#fi_waiting_on` / billing issues block.
3. **View Load from View Billing** may open a **new tab** — resolve the active `Page` (see `resolveViewLoadPageAfterBillingClick` in BT-74454) before constructing `ViewLoadPage` / `LoadBillingPage`.
4. Billing issue **tags** (e.g. Not Deliv. Final, Price Difference) on View Load use **`ViewLoadPage`** helpers scoped to the Waiting On table — do not use `sharedPage.locator` in specs.

`PromptsConfig.REFERENCE_PATTERNS.BILLING_TOGGLE_VIEW_LOAD_VS_VIEW_BILLING` documents the same split for template/snippets.

## Test execution structure (no skipped steps / validations)

1. **Preserve testcase order** — actions and **expected** outcomes from the source sheet (e.g. CSV) appear in the same sequence in generated code.
2. **Every explicit expected** gets an **`expect` / `expect.soft`** or structured alert handling (`validateAlert` / `acceptAllDialogsDuringAction` + assertion on dialog text) — not `console.log` alone.
3. Use **nested `test.step(...)`** titles that reference **step numbers and/or expected text** (e.g. `CSV 53: …`, `Step 5 [CSV 44-48]: …`) so reports map 1:1 to the written case and reviewers can see no step was dropped.
4. Prefer **`PAYABLE_TOGGLE_VALUE`**, **`BILLING_ISSUE_TAGS`**, **`LOAD_STATUS`**, **`ALERT_PATTERNS`** over hardcoded strings in assertions.

## Assertion Values

Never hardcode expected values in assertions. Use:
- `INVOICE_PROCESS.OFFICE`, `AUTOPAY_STATUS.ENABLED`, `PAYABLE_TOGGLE_VALUE.AGENT`, `FINANCE_MESSAGES.LOAD_NOT_INVOICED` from `globalConstants.ts`
- `testData.*` from CSV for dynamic values (rates, amounts, names)

## POM Method JSDoc

Every new POM method must include: `@author AI Agent`, `@created YYYY-MM-DD`, `@param` (if applicable), `@returns` (if applicable), and locator source reference.
